          "entry_id": 2736,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.23978002,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "d on the other side of your mouth for the first few days. For pain, use the over-the-counter painkiller the dentist recommended at your appointment.\n\nContact us if the bleeding has not stopped after f",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2736,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.2052038,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "r if you have ever taken a bisphosphonate such as alendronate (Fosamax) for bone density. These medicines change how the dentist plans an extraction. Do not stop taking them before your appointment un",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2729,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.19108295,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: Which health insurance plans do you accept?\nAnswer: We accept most major insurance providers, including Blue Cross Blue Shield, Aetna, Cigna, UnitedHealthcare, and Medicare. If you're unsure",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2726,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.18538366,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: Do I need a referral from a primary care doctor to book with a specialist?\nAnswer: You can book a visit with any of our practitioners without a referral.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2730,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.18295467,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: What should I do if my insurance isn't listed or I am out-of-network?\nAnswer: You can pay out-of-pocket for your visit, and we can provide you with an itemized receipt to submit to your insu",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2743,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.1701235,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "r blood glucose readings to each review, and bring your inhalers if you have asthma or COPD, so the GP can check your technique.\n\n## Ear wax removal\n\nWe remove ear wax by microsuction, which uses a sm",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2743,
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "similarity_score": 0.16916682,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "hree weeks apart. We do not remove skin tags, moles or other skin lesions for cosmetic reasons.\n\n## Medical examinations for work, driving and sport\n\nWe do not carry out commercial driver (DOT) medica",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2728,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.16562977,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: Do you offer virtual or telehealth consultations?\nAnswer: No, we currently only offer in-person visits at our clinic location.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2732,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.162316,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: When is payment due, and what payment methods do you accept?\nAnswer: Payment is due at the time of service. We accept cash, major credit and debit cards (Visa, Mastercard, American Express),",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2744,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.15912528,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": " a back tooth - $210\n- D2140: silver (amalgam) filling on one surface - $160\n- D7140: simple tooth extraction - $240\n\n## A code you do not recognise\n\nIf your receipt shows a code that is not in this l",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2733,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.15680443,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: What are your clinic hours and locations?\nAnswer: We are open Monday through Saturday from 9:00 AM to 6:00 PM at 15a Willson St. The nearest free parking is a 3-minute walk away at the Mega ",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2744,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.15512711,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Procedure codes and self-pay prices\n\nYour itemized receipt lists each procedure done at your visit by its billing code. Medical procedures use five-digit CPT codes, and dental procedures use CDT cod",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2736,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.14841002,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Dental care guide\n\n## What a dental appointment covers\n\nA routine dental appointment includes an examination of your teeth and gums and a professional cleaning. Fillings and extractions are usually ",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2735,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.14719626,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n\nThis guide lists, plan by plan, the health insurance plans we are in-network with. Insurance companies sell many plans under one brand name, and being in-network with a company",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2737,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.13606188,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Preparing for tests at the clinic\n\nSome tests are done at the clinic during a regular appointment. This guide explains how to prepare for each of them. If your doctor has given you different instruc",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2735,
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "similarity_score": 0.12438776,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": " is not in-network. AARP Medicare Advantage plans from UnitedHealthcare are in-network when the plan is a PPO, and not in-network when it is an HMO.\n\n## Medicare and Medicaid\n\nWe accept Original Medic",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2727,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.12401607,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: What should I bring to my first appointment?\nAnswer: Please bring a valid photo ID, your insurance card, and any relevant prior lab or test results related to your case.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2741,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.11967085,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": " your last name and date of birth. The kiosk cannot take payments: any copay or self-pay amount is paid at the front desk.\n\n## Language interpreters\n\nFree telephone interpreting is available in more t",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2737,
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "similarity_score": 0.118822984,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "have been asked to bring a urine sample, collect a sterile container from the front desk beforehand; household containers can contaminate the sample. Unless you were told otherwise, collect the first ",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2740,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.111942336,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "only the clinic's name, a callback number and your first name - never the reason for the call or any health details.\n\n## Messages we will never send\n\nWe will never ask for your card number, bank detai",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2735,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.111771554,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "re not in-network with Blue Essentials HMO or Blue Advantage HMO plans, because those plans only cover care from their own medical groups.\n\n## Aetna\n\nWe are in-network with Aetna Choice POS II and Aet",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2743,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.11078123,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# General practice services\n\n## Annual physical examination\n\nAn annual physical is a preventive check-up for adults who feel well. It includes a review of your medical history and current medicines; y",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2738,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.10991206,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Vaccinations\n\n## Seasonal flu vaccine\n\nWe give the flu vaccine every year from the start of September until the end of March. Patients aged 65 and over are offered a high-dose vaccine (Fluzone High-",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2742,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.10461197,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "ltation for your personal use, as long as you tell the practitioner before you start. Staff and other patients must not be recorded or photographed.\n\n## How long we keep records\n\nWe keep adult medical",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2731,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.1033749,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: How much will my visit cost if I am paying out-of-pocket?\nAnswer: Out-of-pocket rates are $120 for a General Practitioner (GP) visit, $180 for a Dentist appointment, and $160 for all other s",
          "text_truncated": true
        }
      ],
